You were running down the night streets and armed people loomed behind every corner. The wind in your ears seemed like bullets whizzing by.
But the most important question was what or who made you turn into a wolf. You was absolutely sure that no animal bit or even scratched you. You were confused.
Now there were fewer houses on the street. It looked like the edge of town. You clearly remembered that there were a zoo somewhere near with a wolf cage in it. Currently people were more dangerous to you than wolves, and a crazy idea came to your mind. What if you could lose your pursuers by hiding in the wolf pack at the zoo? At least you'd survive the night. What would happen next you tried not to think of.  
It was easy to hop over the wolf enclosure fence, much easier than the concrete wall. The scared wolves huddled up, looking at you with their teeth bared. It appeared they felt that you were the wrong wolf to mess with, but seeing that you didn't intend to attack, eventually they calmed down and returned to their routine.